deltahdl 0.1.0
SystemVerilog IEEE 1800-2023 simulator and synthesizer

Usage: deltahdl [options] <source-files...>

General:
  -o <name>            Set output name
  --top <module>       Top-level module
  --mintypmax <val>    min:typ:max member: min, typ or max
  --max-generate-iterations <n>
                       Loop generate iteration budget (default 262144)
  -f <file>            Read options from file
  -v <file>            Verilog library file
  -y <dir>             Verilog library directory
  -L <name>            Library search order (repeatable)
  <file>.map           Library map file, read before the sources (33.3.1);
                       lib.map in the working directory when none is named
  +define+<n>=<v>      Define macro
  +incdir+<path>       Include directory
  +<plusarg>           Plusarg for $test$plusargs and $value$plusargs (21.6)
  -Wall -Werror        Warning controls
  --version / --help   Info

Protected envelopes:
  --encrypt            Encrypt the `pragma protect envelopes and write the text
  --protect-key <key>  Key every region is encrypted under
  --protect-named-key <owner>:<name>=<key>
                       Key selecting the regions naming it (repeatable)

Simulation:
  --vcd <file>         Dump VCD waveforms
  --fst <file>         Dump FST waveforms
  --max-time <time>    Maximum simulation time
  --seed <n>           Random seed
  --timescale <t/p>    Override default timescale
  --vpi-compat-mode <mode>
                       Default VPI compatibility mode (36.12.2.2):
                       1364v1995, 1364v2001, 1364v2005, 1800v2005, 1800v2009
  --negative-timing-checks
                       Accept negative $setuphold/$recrem limits (31.9.4)
  --no-timing-checks   Turn every timing check off (31.9.4)
  -D <name>[=<value>]  Define preprocessor macro
  --lint-only          Parse and elaborate only
  --parse-only         Parse only
  --dump-ast           Print AST to stdout
  --dump-ir            Print RTLIR to stdout

Synthesis:
  --synth              Synthesis mode
  --target <name>      Target technology
  --lut-size <n>       LUT input count (default 4)
  --lib <file>         Liberty timing library
  --config <name>      Configuration to bind (33.5.4)
  --load-lib <file>    Precompiled library to bind from
  --precompile-into <library>
                       Library to compile sources into
  --precompile-out <file>
                       File the precompiled cells go to
  --format <fmt>       Output format (blif/verilog/json/edif)
  --no-opt             Skip optimization passes
  --area               Area-oriented optimization
  --delay              Delay-oriented optimization
  --retime             Enable register retiming
  --dump-aig           Print AIG to stdout
